      "mergeID": "65c10bed41a305a5770ecc9a",
      "mergedPostDetails": "While it is known at the time of posting that the development team is working to overhaul the camera functions I figure that for those that make content, shows, etc. within VRChat it would be greatly beneficial for the the camera to have a lot more features, two of which may help out the virtual filmers quite a bit: a dolly track system akin to how cinemachine works, and adding more pins so that it would be easier for virtual film makers to have more spots to put them. For the new pin system in order to add a pin there would be a + icon to generate a pin, the maximum allowable pins should be up to 10 until there could be better ways of optimizing the pins later down the line if needed. When placing pins you can optionally have an indicator for how you want them to behave in the dolly track, which pin is A and if it goes to that pin we call B. Either way it should be a thing to be considered",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Add more pins and a dolly system for VRChat Cameras",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "62defb4e82494544a24f91b7",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm not sure I need the rest of that. But more pins would be nice.  There seems to be room for 2 more pin buttons for a total of 5 easily without changing other things.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
